From 38c5d05a7151d74075b52f226253518d928faf87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Schmitt <max@schmitt.mx>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 05:32:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] apprt/embedded: headless platform for offscreen embedding
 (macOS)

GHOSTTY_PLATFORM_HEADLESS: a surface with no NSView. The Metal
backend's IOSurfaceLayer already works standalone (the view was only
a place to hang the layer), so headless skips the attach and sizes
the layer directly via the new Metal.setLayerSize().

ghostty_surface_headless_frame() returns the last presented IOSurface
(retained +1 for the caller) with size/scale, so embedders can read
frames or import them into their own compositor (e.g. Electron's
sharedTexture module) without any view hierarchy. Ghostty
triple-buffers: the returned surface is reused two presents later, so
callers must copy or import promptly (documented on the API).

Headless requires the Metal backend today; surface_new returns
error.UnsupportedPlatform on non-Darwin targets instead of panicking
at the first GL call.
---
 include/ghostty.h      | 21 +++++++++
 src/apprt/embedded.zig | 99 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/renderer/Metal.zig | 40 ++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 153 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

